# The analyzers that answer an unsatisfied push2u dependency in a context where this starter's own
# startup refusals never ran: a missing PushSender, and a missing EndpointPolicy — the bean a service
# that only accepts subscriptions injects, in the one deployment shape that builds no sender for the
# sender's own refusal to run inside. Their precedence over Spring Boot's own missing-bean analyzer
# is declared on each class with @Order, not taken from this file's position on the classpath.
org.springframework.boot.diagnostics.FailureAnalyzer=\
com.the13haven.push2u.spring.MissingPushSenderFailureAnalyzer,\
com.the13haven.push2u.spring.MissingEndpointPolicyFailureAnalyzer
